        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.231,
            0.408,
            0.411,
            0.463
          ],
          "content": "I wonder how the level of a coloured liquid is measured?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.446,
            0.362,
            0.744,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": "Once it reaches the required level—that is, 50 mL— transfer this water to the required container."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.427,
            0.444,
            0.744,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": "In case of coloured liquids the mark on the measuring cylinder should coincide with the top of the meniscus!"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.521,
            0.743,
            0.564
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Determining volume of solid objects with regular shapes"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.58,
            0.503,
            0.605
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 9.6: Let us calculate"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.616,
            0.743,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": "**Collect** various objects with a cuboid shapes, such as a notebook, a shoe box, or a dice."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.654,
            0.743,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": "z Measure the length (l), width (w), and height (h) of the objects using a scale. Suppose the length of the notebook is 25 cm, the width is 18 cm, and the height is 2 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.711,
            0.681,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": "z **Calculate** the volume by using the following formula."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.338,
            0.731,
            0.52,
            0.749
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{Volume} = l \\times w \\times h",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.226,
            0.751,
            0.632,
            0.77
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{Volume}=25\\mathrm{~cm}\\times18\\mathrm{~cm}\\times2\\mathrm{~cm}=900\\mathrm{~cm}^{3}",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.772,
            0.409,
            0.792
          ],
          "content": "z Record in your notebook."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.802,
            0.722,
            0.823
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Determining volume of objects with irregular shapes"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.826,
            0.744,
            0.901
          ],
          "content": "Imagine you have an object, like a stone, that does not have a regular shape. To calculate its density, the main challenge is to find its volume. Let us learn how the volume of a solid with an irregular shape can be determined."
        },
        {
